/*
:name: clock_or_data
:type: error
:tolg: 1
:error: (not a clock operation)
*/
// todo/livehd/2f-latch M9 — NOTHING MAY BE DONE TO A CLOCK except a recognized
// clock operation. A clock may be GATED (`clk and en`) or INVERTED (`not clk`);
// both lower to a `Clock_cell` that every consumer knows how to interpret.
//
// `clk or sel` is neither. It has no meaning as a clock, and getting it wrong
// is SILENT rather than loud: a step-granular formal encoder has no
// clock-identity model, so an OR of a clock with data looks exactly like the
// bare clock and the design came back PROVEN equal to an ungated one. Catch it
// at compile time, where the source span still exists to point at.
//
// The legal forms are exercised elsewhere: `clk and en` in
// tests/equiv/latch_icg.prp, `not clk` wherever a negedge flop appears.
pub mod bad_clock(clk:bool, sel:bool, d:u8) -> (q:u8@[1]) {
  wire gclk:bool = nil
  gclk = clk or sel
  reg f:u8:[clock_pin=ref gclk] = 0
  q = f
  f = d
}
